    "sample": {
      "size": 24,
      "text": "Ratna changes the look only. Screens, steps, words, permissions and money rules are Concept A's. All names, plates and amounts are illustrative sample data from the design briefs (Thu 22 Oct 2026). Sinhala labels are drafts for SNS review. Vehicle pictures are line outlines until real car photos are added.",
      "w": 380,
      "x": 1990,
      "y": 1980
    },
    "rowVD": {
      "x": 0,
      "y": 12960,
      "text": "Vehicle detail — every card opens this",
      "kind": "title1",
      "maxW": 3580
    },
    "vdNote": {
      "x": 3660,
      "y": 13240,
      "w": 400,
      "text": "Layout B, chosen 23 Oct. Owner sees everything; staff lose the two owner-only sections and the partner’s name, everywhere including history. The action changes with status (board 14). Unknown facts stay unknown: the revenue licence date and the next service were never recorded, so they show as dashed “add” rows, not invented dates.",
      "fill": "yellow",
      "size": 24
    },
    "rowRent": {
      "x": 0,
      "y": 16080,
      "text": "Rentals — what needs doing, and one rental in full",
      "kind": "title1",
      "maxW": 4940
    },
    "rentNote": {
      "x": 5020,
      "y": 16360,
      "w": 400,
      "text": "Layout B, chosen 23 Oct: who and which car on the left, the money on the right. Staff on the phone see the same rental without the owner-only split and without the partner’s name. An open rental (board 19) shows the bill so far: extra km and any late charge stay “at return”, and no late fee runs on its own. Customer names appear only where the sample data has one.",
      "fill": "yellow",
      "size": 24
    },
    "rowCust": {
      "x": 0,
      "y": 18780,
      "text": "Customers — who owes, and one customer in full",
      "kind": "title1",
      "maxW": 3580
    },
    "custNote": {
      "x": 3660,
      "y": 19060,
      "w": 400,
      "text": "Decided 23 Oct: staff see full NIC and phone numbers (no masking). The sample data has no real numbers, so 199012345678 and 077 123 4567 are dummy placeholders, also now on the new-rental screen (board 7). No ratings or trust scores, by the system design. Old debt shows automatically as a warning; flags are added by staff with a reason. Write-off stays with authorised people.",
      "fill": "yellow",
      "size": 24
    },
    "rowMC": {
      "x": 0,
      "y": 21420,
      "text": "Morning check — 7:30, both directions",
      "kind": "title1",
      "maxW": 2690
    },
    "mcNote": {
      "x": 2770,
      "y": 21700,
      "w": 400,
      "fill": "yellow",
      "size": 24,
      "text": "Built straight from the spec (S6, 23 Oct). List A: the 18 cars the records place at the branch at 7:30, grouped by model so staff walk the yard once; each gets Found / Not here. List B (board 26): a car in the yard whose record says rented, repair or unavailable. The sample day has no such case, so CAA 9083 there is illustrative. Any mismatch opens a discrepancy that needs an explanation plus a confirmed status, closed by a permitted person (a Settings permission, not decided here). The sample data names no checker; Nimal is illustrative, and per-car tap times are not recorded, so none are shown."
    }
